    "done_when": "tests/test_a_torn_transcript_line_does_not_break_a_board_read.py writes, in a temporary directory, a transcript of whole assistant lines followed by a last line torn in the middle of a multi-byte character (for example ending b'\"h\\xc3'). It asserts that dispatch_accounting._jsonl_events yields every whole line's event and raises nothing. It shrinks directory._TRANSCRIPT_TAIL_SIZES in the test so the board's context-use read falls through to the forward read, as the existing context-use test does, and asserts that the read returns the last whole request rather than raising. Both cases fail at the base. Negative control, applied and logged to logs/negative-control.log under the run directory: restore strict decoding in _jsonl_events, and both cases fail. baseline_suite and after_suite are run with the project's armed suite command at the base and the head, each log naming its revision, tree and literal command and ending EXIT=. Every test file that imports reckon.crew.dispatch_accounting or reckon.crew.directory adds no failure against a base arm: run both arms from git archive extractions on node-local disk with the main checkout's .env linked, -n 6 at most, and re-run any id that differs serially. Gate and arm logs go under the run directory. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the staged paths. Run every gate in the foreground on the fleet allocation.",
